Locality:
  At any given moment, a program is likely to be accessing
    only a small part of its memory.
  Code:
    Mostly accessed sequentially.
    Loops and 'if' (branches) jump around only a little usually.
  Data:
    video editing is memory intensive, and we need to load everything into memory(the whole video)
    a lot of programs that we write end up using the same data repeatedly.
  ..Temporal locality:
    recently used data is likely to be reused (i.e., loops)
  ..Spatial locality:
    governed by the idea that the next data we use is probably nearby previous data you used(e.g., an array/struct)
    (linked list violate spatial locality).
  
